# LOOP (SEL on HOME): the loop's layers, a row each. SELECT: the layer. The knobs: its LEVEL, its
# SOUND (as played, or one of VOX's four for all its notes), its OCTAVE, MUTE. SEL twice takes a layer out,
# the ones over it moving down with their settings. Two layers of the same note sound as two (one an octave
# up, in another sound). All of it is saved with the loop. With no loop, the page says so.
wait 1000
tap SEL
wait 100
expect view 8
shot loop_empty.png
turn K1 2
tap HOME
expect view 0
tap REC
key w2 down
wait 2600
tap REC
wait 100
key w2 up
expect looper 2
tap REC
key w2 down
wait 2400
key w2 up
wait 300
tap REC
wait 100
expect layers 2
tap SEL
wait 100
expect view 8
expect lrow 1
expect lay10 100
turn SELECT 1
expect lrow 2
turn K2 2
turn K3 1
wait 200
expect lay21 2
expect lay22 2
wait 3000
expect vox_sounds 3
shot loop_layers.png
turn K1 -10
wait 100
expect lay20 80
turn SELECT -1
turn K4 1
wait 3400
expect lay13 1
expect vox_sounds 2
turn K4 -1
wait 3000
expect lay13 0
expect vox_sounds 3
tap SAVE
wait 500
expect store_writes >0
reboot
wait 3000
expect layers 2
expect lay20 80
expect lay21 2
expect lay22 2
tap SEL
wait 100
tap SEL
wait 100
expect layers 2
tap SEL
wait 300
expect layers 1
expect lay10 80
expect lay11 2
expect lay12 2
wait 3000
expect vox_sounds 2
tap SEL
wait 100
tap SEL
wait 300
expect looper 0
expect vox_sounds 0
expect clips 0
